  "id": "COMPOUND:32301 - PROTEIN:6336",
  "verbalization": "Dodonolide is implicated in the pathway leading to Thrombopoietin through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Dodonolide directly targets Hepatocytes, which in turn are targets of other compounds, including (4S,5S)-5-[(1R,2R)-2-Hydroxy-2-Methyl-5-Oxocyclopent-3-En-1-Yl]-3-Methylidene-4-(3-Oxobutyl)Oxolan-2-One and (5R,7S,8S)-5-hydroxy-4-methoxy-7,8-dimethyl-7,8-dihydro-5H-pyrano[4,3-b]pyran-2-one. These secondary targets ultimately direct their activity toward Thrombopoietin. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Dodonolide may influence cellular processes in Hepatocytes, which in turn modulate Thrombopoietin production. The evidence supports a link between Dodonolide and Thrombopoietin through a chain of molecular interactions involving Hepatocytes and their target compounds.",
